---
/**
 * The stage the whole page sits on: one fixed canvas, one annotation layer the
 * 3D scene projects into, one CSS sky for machines without WebGL, and the veil
 * the opening waits behind. The DOM here is identical in every case — only the
 * classes on <html> decide what is visible.
 */
---

<div class="stage" data-stage>
  <div class="stage__fallback" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <canvas class="stage__canvas" data-canvas aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
  <div class="stage__annotations" data-annotations aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="veil" data-veil aria-hidden="true"><span class="veil__label">ORBITAL</span></div>
</div>

<p class="sr-only">
  A live model of the Solar System. The scene shows Earth, the Moon, Mars, the asteroid belt,
  Jupiter and the Sun at their real positions for the current date. Scrolling moves one continuous
  camera from a window above Earth to the surface of the Sun; the date control near the end moves
  every world along its orbit. All copy on this page is available as text below.
</p>
